            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Joanne and Kevin put all their marbles in a bag. ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\frac{3}{5}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " of the marbles belong to Joanne.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p104-q26-changes",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In a competition Kevin doubled the number of marbles that he owned, and Joanne won 6 more, so that now they had an equal number of marbles.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p104-q26-request",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How many marbles did they each have originally?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Kevin: 12 marbles; Joanne: 18 marbles.",
      "worked": "Let $J$ and $K$ be Joanne’s and Kevin’s original numbers of marbles. Joanne owned $\\frac35$ of the total and Kevin owned $\\frac25$, so $J=\\frac32K$. Afterwards, $J+6=2K$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac32K+6&=2K\\\\3K+12&=4K\\\\12&=K\\\\J&=\\frac32K\\\\&=\\frac32(12)\\\\&=18\\end{align*}$$\nKevin had 12 marbles and Joanne had 18 marbles.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
